    "resident_plateau_logical_byte_rate_per_s": 10138304048892.283,
    "selection_rule": "At each measured footprint retain the minimum median logical byte rate across the two independent clock-gated captures on the owned device. The endpoints are measured extremes, not a fit: the resident plateau is the largest conservative rate at or below 40.5 MiB (0.675x L2, the A800 27/40 ratio) and the DRAM asymptote the smallest at or above 81.0 MiB (1.35x L2, the A800 54/40 ratio). A stream serving a fraction f of its bytes from DRAM and the rest from L2 takes (1-f)/resident_plateau + f/dram_asymptote per byte, so inverting the measured rate gives f directly. The running maximum over increasing footprint keeps the published fraction monotone and conservative against measurement noise; no intermediate value is fitted.",
    "spread_gate_note": "The A800 runner aborts a capture whose footprint trial spread exceeds 8 percent. On H200 the 45..54 MiB transition exceeds it in every capture (also with 256 warm-up passes), so the H200 runner records the footprints instead (provenance.captures[].spread_gate_exceeded_footprints_mib) and the median rate is used as on A800."
  },
